# Standing rules

These rules apply to every task in this repo. Follow them even when the user does not repeat them. Drop a rule only when the user explicitly says to drop it.

## Before you implement

1. Treat the files in `.cursor/rules/` as the project brief. Cursor injects `alwaysApply` rules into context, so do not re-read them from disk unless you are editing them.
2. Do not scan the repository to rediscover conventions already stated in these rules.
3. Open only the files the current task needs. Search by name or symbol before listing directories.
4. If a convention is missing here, learn it from the files the task touches. Do not widen the search to the rest of the repo.

## How new rules are stored

- One concern per file, under `.cursor/rules/`, as `.mdc`.
- Rules for every task: `alwaysApply: true`, no globs, kept short.
- Rules for some files only: `alwaysApply: false` plus a `globs` pattern, so they load only when those files are in play.
- Add a new short rule instead of growing this file. Keep each rule under 50 lines.
